{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>and give you rest</b> — and give you rest." "<b>delights</b> — when he receives instruction."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The lemma is Ibn Ezra's interpretive rendering of the verse's ויניחך; the gloss defines it as 'give you rest.'", 1 "Ibn Ezra reads מעדנים in light of the root עדן in the sense of 'pleasant/delight,' glossed here as the circumstance in which the son accepts discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:24.993981501Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}